/target/
# `nix build` 在当前目录留下的输出链接。
/result
/result-*
# Every platform keeps its build output in its own target/ (platforms/ios/target/sim-shots, a stray platforms/target/linux), and checks that import sibling modules leave bytecode caches next to them. Neither should depend on a contributor's global ignore file.
/platforms/*/target/
/platforms/target/
__pycache__/
.build/
node_modules/
dist/
.DS_Store
*.local
.env
.env.*
!Cargo.lock
!pnpm-lock.yaml
/apps/desktop/src-tauri/gen/*
!/apps/desktop/src-tauri/gen/android/
!/apps/desktop/src-tauri/gen/apple/
/platforms/ios/Pods/
/platforms/ios/MSIMEClient.xcworkspace/
/platforms/harmony/.hvigor/
/platforms/harmony/entry/build/
/platforms/harmony/entry/libs/
# No trailing slash: staging resources into a worktree by symlinking this path instead of copying
# 181 MB is an obvious thing to do on a full disk, and a directory-only rule does not match the
# symlink. One got committed that way, pointing at an absolute path on one machine.
/platforms/harmony/entry/src/main/resources/resfile
# The HarmonyOS settings page, built from packages/ui by platforms/harmony/stage-settings.sh before every HAP build.
/platforms/harmony/entry/src/main/resources/rawfile/settings/
oh_modules/
local.properties
# Regenerated by DevEco on every build and resolves a single in-tree path
# dependency, so a tracked copy only ever shows up as a dirty working tree.
/platforms/harmony/entry/oh-package-lock.json5

# Local editor and coding-agent state. Contributor machines differ; none of it
# describes the project.
tasks/
.gitnexus
.vscode/
.idea/
# Skills are the exception the comment above asks for: they describe how to build and launch this project, not how one contributor's machine is set up, and they are worth no less than the prose in AGENTS.md. Everything else under .claude/ stays out — settings.local.json and the scheduler lock are per-machine state.
#
# Each skill lives in .agents/skills/, which Codex and other agents read; .claude/skills/ only holds a relative symlink per skill, because Claude Code looks nowhere else. A new skill goes into .agents/skills/ and gets its link here.
#
# The contents are excluded rather than the directory: git will not re-include a path whose parent directory is itself excluded, so `.claude/` plus a negation silently keeps ignoring the skills.
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/

# Local audit and artifact reports must never enter a source release.
.tmp-*
*.report.html

# 决策看板由 pnpm run init-board / bundle-board 随时从 .agents/notes 重新生成，不进版本库。
/board.html
/demo.html

# Nothing reads vendor/ any more: the input engine is crates/engine. Checkouts made before that still hold the fetched C++ Engine tree (or a link to one) there, so it stays ignored rather than showing up as thousands of untracked files a broad `git add` would commit. Delete the directory by hand.
/vendor/

# Downloaded neural sentence weights are reproducible build output; their lock and attribution
# stay tracked in resources/neural-model.lock.json and docs/third-party.md.
/target/neural-model/*.safetensors

# The native host's Gradle project: its build directories and daemon caches are per-machine, and the
# .gradle caches hold absolute paths and lock files that mean nothing on another checkout.
/platforms/android/gradle-app/.gradle/
/platforms/android/gradle-app/build/
/platforms/android/gradle-app/app/build/
